.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Provides an extended and strongly typed comparison contract for \fBSystemEx\fP\&. 

Unlike System\&.IComparable<T>, which returns an integer (-1, 0, +1), this interface uses the explicit \fBCompareResult\fP enumeration\&. This makes comparison outcomes easier to interpret and avoids ambiguity, especially in low‑level or domain‑specific types\&.

.PP
\fBCompatibility with IComparable<T>:\fP
.br
 Since \fBCompareResult\fP is backed by an integer, any type can implement both interfaces simultaneously\&. The standard CompareTo method can simply cast the extended result: 

.PP
.PP
.nf
public sealed class Foo : IComparableEx&lt;Foo&gt;, IComparable&lt;Foo&gt;
{
    public CompareResult CompareTo(Foo other)
    {
        // Custom comparison logic\&.\&.\&.
        return CompareResult\&.Equal;
    }

    int IComparable&lt;Foo&gt;\&.CompareTo(Foo other)
    {
        // Cast the extended comparison result to an int\&.
        return (int)CompareTo(other);
    }
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
This interface is intentionally generic and can be implemented by any type: numeric primitives, geometric structures, colors, states, or any other domain‑specific objects requiring deterministic comparison semantics\&. 

.PP
